  <!-- WHAT IS PBP -->
  <section class="section" id="what-is-pbp">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-label">Play-by-Post</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Collaborative storytelling at your own pace</h2>
      <div class="pbp-grid">
        <div class="pbp-text">
          <p>
            Play-by-post (PbP) is a form of roleplaying where participants write
            their characters' actions, dialogue, and inner thoughts in a shared
            thread — building a story together, one post at a time.
          </p>
          <p>
            Unlike tabletop sessions that require everyone online at the same
            moment, PbP is asynchronous. A writer in Tokyo and a writer in
            Toronto can share the same adventure without ever needing to find a
            common evening.
          </p>
          <p>
            The format rewards craft: players edit, revise, and illustrate their
            posts. Stories accumulate into archives that read like novels.
            Communities grow around rich fictional worlds that can last for years.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="pbp-callouts">
          <div class="callout">
            <div class="callout-icon">✦</div>
            <div>
              <strong>Asynchronous by nature</strong>
              <p>Post when inspiration strikes — no session scheduling required.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="callout">
            <div class="callout-icon">✦</div>
            <div>
              <strong>Writing as the medium</strong>
              <p>Characters come alive through prose, not dice rolls alone.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="callout">
            <div class="callout-icon">✦</div>
            <div>
              <strong>Living archives</strong>
              <p>Years of collaborative fiction, searchable and preserved.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

