  <!-- WHY CUENTO -->
  <section class="section" id="features">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-label">Why Cuento</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Not a forum. Not a wiki.<br />Something built for the game.</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        General-purpose forum software was designed for discussion threads,
        not collaborative fiction. Cuento replaces the patchwork of plugins,
        spreadsheets, and Discord servers that most PbP communities rely on.
      </p>
      <div class="compare-grid">
        <div class="compare-col compare-col--other">
          <h3>Standard forum software</h3>
          <ul class="compare-list">
            <li>Characters tracked in profile bios or external sheets</li>
            <li>No concept of a "game" or "episode" — just categories</li>
            <li>Moderation built for spam, not collaborative storytelling</li>
            <li>No AI tools — narration notes live in a separate doc</li>
            <li>Direct messages are plaintext and not role-aware</li>
            <li>Search is full-text only — no semantic "find scenes like this"</li>
            <li>Hosting means maintaining generic forum stack + plugins</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-col compare-col--cuento">
          <h3>Cuento</h3>
          <ul class="compare-list">
            <li>First-class character system with custom fields, masks, and galleries</li>
            <li>Episodes and games as native objects — timelines, digests, arcs</li>
            <li>Subforum-level permissions with per-character role rules</li>
            <li>Built-in AI: lore Q&A with cited sources, weekly game digest, post proofreader</li>
            <li>Semantic + full-text search across lore and posts</li>
            <li>WYSIWYG post editor with BBCode and live preview</li>
            <li>Real-time notifications for posts, mentions, and messages</li>
            <li>Instant character claim from wanted listings</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

